# build output
#
# `/bin/` is anchored to the repository root. The fixture builds its driver and
# the reference checker into testdata/kvfixture/bin/, where a Windows build is
# caught by *.exe below and a Linux one (`loadgen`, no extension) was not.
/bin/
**/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out

# PRO-THESIS runtime state.
# NOTE: .prothesis/oracles/, .prothesis/lock and .prothesis/regressions/ are NOT ignored.
# Per invariant I6 and anti-gaming rule 4, oracles, the lock manifest and the regression
# corpus are first-class committed artifacts. Only transient run output is ignored.
**/.prothesis/runs/
**/.prothesis/corpus/
**/.prothesis/tmp/
# Clustering engine reports: derived, regenerable from the corpus and registry.
**/.prothesis/cluster_features.csv
**/.prothesis/cluster_manifest.json
**/.prothesis/cluster_report.yaml
**/.prothesis/taxonomy_report.yaml

# Go workspace
go.work
go.work.sum
vendor/

# Python bytecode from the observation bundle's crosscheck.py
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The author's separate distadv / web-console project. It is a repository of its
# own that happens to sit inside this directory; nothing in it is part of
# PRO-THESIS (D-075 records what was ported from it).
GLM Build/
